{"name":"Nail Polish Pink","hex":"#bd4e84","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nail","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The horny plate or appendage at the ends of the digits of various animals, including most reptiles, birds, and mammals (both nonhuman and human).","The thin, flat type of such a plate on the fingers and toes of humans, chimpanzees and some other primates."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fix (an object) to another object using a nail.","To drive a nail."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nail"},{"term":"polish","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A substance used to polish.","Cleanliness; smoothness, shininess."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To shine; to make a surface very smooth or shiny by rubbing, cleaning, or grinding.","To refine; remove imperfections from."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/polish"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nail (anatomy)","blocks":[{"text":"A nail is a protective plate characteristically found at the tip of the digits of almost all primates, homologous to the claws in other tetrapod animals. Fingernails and toenails are made of a tough rigid protein called alpha-keratin, a polymer also found in the claws, hooves, and horns of vertebrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Nail_svg_hariadhi.svg/330px-Nail_svg_hariadhi.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nail_(anatomy)","wikidata":"Q36864"},{"title":"Nail polish","blocks":[{"text":"Nail polish is a lacquer that can be applied to the human fingernails or toenails to decorate and protect the nail plates. The formula has been revised repeatedly to enhance its decorative properties, to be safer for the consumer to use, and to suppress cracking or peeling. Nail polish consists of a mix of an organic polymer and several other components that give it colors and textures. Nail polishes come in all color shades and play a significant part in manicures and pedicures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Polished_purple_nails_with_nail_art_on.jpg/330px-Polished_purple_nails_with_nail_art_on.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nail_polish","wikidata":"Q223807"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Human_nail_anatomy.jpg/500px-Human_nail_anatomy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Human_nail_anatomy.jpg/1280px-Human_nail_anatomy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Human_nail_anatomy.jpg/500px-Human_nail_anatomy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A. Nail plate; B. lunula; C. root; D. sinus; E. matrix; F. nail bed; G. hyponychium; H. free margin","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/